    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0329" n="239" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2176</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-01T15:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1, 1918, 3
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 2, 9 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following the occupation of Vladivostok by the Czech forces on the 29th, fully
                    reported by Admiral Knight and Caldwell,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d306-f1"/> the
                    French Government to-day requested the Japanese Government to lend to the Czech
                    army 30 machine guns and a number of mountain batteries with the necessary
                    ammunition to prevent a possible counter attack by the Red Guard. The Japanese
                    Government is considering this request, but appears inclined to answer that it
                    does not feel justified in taking any action until the Allies and the United
                    States are agreed on a general plan to be adopted in meeting the situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
